From: CubieBoard4 Build <build@cubieboard4>
Date: Mon, 1 Jan 2024 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] mmc: sunxi: Pre-enable CLK after hardware reset

The A80 (sun9i) MMC controller's CLKCR register is not cleared by
SDXC_HARDWARE_RESET issued in sunxi_mmc_reset_host(). Channels that
were initialised by U-Boot retain SDXC_CARD_CLOCK_ON=1 from that
initialisation, so the first UPCLK_ONLY command in oclk_onoff()
succeeds immediately.

However, channels that U-Boot never touches (e.g. the SDIO slot used
for a WiFi chip) have CLKCR=0 at power-on.  When sunxi_mmc_reset_host()
is called on such a channel CLKCR remains zero; the subsequent
UPCLK_ONLY command then hangs for the full 750 ms timeout because the
hardware never asserts the clock line when SDXC_CARD_CLOCK_ON=0.  This
sets host->ferror, permanently disabling the controller and preventing
any SDIO/WiFi device from being probed.

Fix this by writing SDXC_CARD_CLOCK_ON into CLKCR immediately after
the hardware reset in sunxi_mmc_init_host().  The divider and other
fields in CLKCR will be reprogrammed by sunxi_mmc_clk_set_rate() once
a card is detected.  This mirrors the explicit workaround present in
U-Boot's drivers/mmc/sunxi_mmc.c.

Fixes WiFi (BCM4330 SDIO on mmc@1c10000) failing to initialise on
Allwinner A80 (CubieBoard4) with "fatal err update clk timeout".

Signed-off-by: CubieBoard4 Build <build@cubieboard4>
---
 drivers/mmc/host/sunxi-mmc.c | 16 +++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/mmc/host/sunxi-mmc.c b/drivers/mmc/host/sunxi-mmc.c
--- a/drivers/mmc/host/sunxi-mmc.c	2024-01-01 00:00:00.000000000 +0000
+++ b/drivers/mmc/host/sunxi-mmc.c	2024-01-01 00:00:01.000000000 +0000
@@ -328,9 +328,23 @@
 	if (sunxi_mmc_reset_host(host))
 		return -EIO;
 
-	/*
-	 * Burst 8 transfers, RX trigger level: 7, TX trigger level: 8
-	 *
-	 * TODO: sun9i has a larger FIFO and supports higher trigger values
+	/*
+	 * After SDXC_HARDWARE_RESET the CLKCR register is not reset by the
+	 * hardware, so it retains whatever value it had.  If this channel was
+	 * never initialised before (e.g. a WiFi SDIO slot that U-Boot never
+	 * touched) CLKCR will be zero, meaning SDXC_CARD_CLOCK_ON = 0.  A
+	 * subsequent UPCLK_ONLY command issued by sunxi_mmc_oclk_onoff() will
+	 * then hang forever: the hardware waits for the clock line to toggle
+	 * but the clock is gated.  Pre-set SDXC_CARD_CLOCK_ON here so the
+	 * first UPCLK_ONLY can complete.  The divider bits will be
+	 * reprogrammed by sunxi_mmc_clk_set_rate() shortly after.
+	 * This mirrors the workaround in U-Boot's drivers/mmc/sunxi_mmc.c.
+	 */
+	mmc_writel(host, REG_CLKCR, SDXC_CARD_CLOCK_ON);
+
+	/*
+	 * Burst 8 transfers, RX trigger level: 7, TX trigger level: 8
+	 *
+	 * TODO: sun9i has a larger FIFO and supports higher trigger values
 	 */
 	mmc_writel(host, REG_FTRGL, 0x20070008);
